John Gibson <jgibsonNO@SPAMshakethebaby.com> wrote:

> Are hobbits restricted in dual-wielding weapons as well?  Or can they 
> run around with two long swords (which is probably just as hard as 
> carrying a battle axe)?

No restrictions at present.  On my "todo" list was forcing hobbits to
use some of the larger weapons like long swords in both hands, which
would effectively prevent dual-wielding long swords and the like, but
still allow them to use two short swords or daggers or whatever.  In
fact, that's why I gave hobbit knights a "hobbit long sword", which is
smaller and could realistically be used one-handed by a hobbit (but
still uses the long sword skill).

What I'm not certain of is how to implement it.  I could maybe simply
have a list of weapons that must be used two-handed by small
creatures, and check the list every time a hobbit tries to wield one,
but this is cumbersome and inflexible.  Perhaps it could be based on
weapon weight, so that if a weapon weighs a certain amount or more,
then it must be used two-handed by hobbits or other small creatures.


